From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*drepaną||to strike, push, beat}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{m|ine-pro|*dhrebh-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*dhreb-||to crack, crush, kill}}; cognate with Old English {{m|ang|drepan}}, German {{m|de|treffen||hit, meet}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb|drap|drápu|drepinn}}

# to [[beat]], to [[hit]], to [[push]], to [[knock]]
# to [[kill]], to [[slay]]
# to [[capture]] (''e.g. in chess'')

